Subject: [PATCH] nss: do not republish or trigger coredump on an empty write

proc_dointvec can return success without assigning a value for a zero-length
write. In that case the call-local snapshot is not a new policy or command.
Do not overwrite a concurrent policy update or trigger an old dump request.

Nonempty writes, parser errors and reads retain their existing semantics.
This does not resolve ignored nonempty strict-offset writes, asynchronous
callback retirement, or the broader firmware ownership contract.

--- a/nss_init.c
+++ b/nss_init.c
@@ -579,7 +579,7 @@ static int nss_coredump_handler(const struct ctl_table *ctl, int write, void __user
 
 	request.data = &coredump;
 	ret = proc_dointvec(&request, write, buffer, lenp, ppos);
-	if (ret || !write)
+	if (ret || !write || !*lenp)
 		return ret;
 	if (nss_ctl_debug && coredump == 1 && !nss_sysctl_ctx_ready(nss_ctx))
 		return -ENODEV;
